          "text": "Clinical Indication:\nRoutine EEG for drug-responsive genetic focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 18, occurring approximately twice yearly. Etiology is attributed to a causative PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. Current antiseizure medications are zonisamide and levetiracetam.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine digital scalp EEG recording using the International 10–20 electrode placement system.\n\nFindings:\nWaveform-level EEG findings were not provided; therefore, background activity, interictal abnormalities, and ictal activity cannot be characterized.\n\nImpression:\nEEG interpretation is indeterminate in the absence of waveform findings. No conclusions regarding interictal epileptiform activity, electrographic seizures, or localization can be made from the supplied information.",
